dialogue is: {{ [doctor] Hi, Carolyn. How are you today?
[patient] I'm doing alright, thank you. How are you?
[doctor] I'm doing well, thank you. I see that you're here for a follow-up of your chronic problem. Can you tell me a little bit about what's going on with you?
[patient] Sure. I've been having some problems with my osteoarthritis. It's been flaring up a little lately, and I was hoping we could talk about that, primarily in my elbows.
[doctor] Okay. So, you're having some issues with your elbows?
[patient] Yes, my right elbow bothers me more than my left elbow, but I'm sitting at the computer a lot, so I'm not sure if it's just from sitting there all day.
[doctor] I see. And how often are you sitting at the computer?
[patient] All day. I work in the office, so I'm sitting at the computer all day.
[doctor] Okay. And are you doing a lot of typing or writing?
[patient] I'm typing, mostly typing.
[doctor] Okay. And any other joints that are bothering you?
[patient] No, just my elbows.
[doctor] Alright. And any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] Yes, I do get a little numbness and tingling in my hands. I try to shake it out to relieve it.
[doctor] Okay. Have you noticed any other issues with your joints, like any swelling or redness?
[patient] No, not really.
[doctor] Alright. How about any other problems with your joints?
[patient] No, just my elbows.
[doctor] Okay. How about your gout? Any issues with that?
[patient] No, I haven't had any problems with gout since my last episode about 3 months ago.
[doctor] Okay. How about your psoriasis? How is that doing?
[patient] It's under control. I haven't had any major issues with that either.
[doctor] Alright. Do you have any other symptoms or issues that I should know about?
[patient] No, that's about it.
[doctor] Okay. Let's do a quick physical exam. Let's start with your neck. Any swelling or tenderness there?
[patient] No, none.
[doctor] Alright. Let's listen to your lungs. Any wheezes, rales, or rhonchi?
[patient] No, none.
[doctor] Let's listen to your heart. Any irregular heartbeat?
[patient] No, my heart is fine.
[doctor] Okay. Let's check your abdomen. Any tenderness there?
[patient] No, it's fine.
[doctor] Alright. Let's check your joints. I'm going to press on your right elbow. Does that hurt?
[patient] Yes, it does.
[doctor] Okay. I'm going to press on your left elbow. Does that hurt?
[patient] No, it doesn't.
[doctor] Alright. Let's check your lower extremities. Any swelling or redness there?
[patient] No, none.
[doctor] Okay. Let's check your right elbow again. I'm going to bend your elbow and see if that hurts.
[patient] Yes, it does.
[doctor] Okay. I'm going to straighten your elbow and see if that hurts.
[patient] Yes, it does.
[doctor] Alright. Any pain with pronation and supination?
[patient] Yes, that hurts too.
[doctor] Okay. Any pain with flexion and extension of your right arm?
[patient] Yes, that hurts.
[doctor] Alright. Let's check your left elbow again. I'm going to bend your left elbow and see if that hurts.
[patient] No, it doesn't.
[doctor] Okay. I'm going to straighten your left elbow and see if that hurts.
[patient] No, it doesn't.
[doctor] Alright. Let's check your left elbow again. Any pain with pronation and supination?
[patient] No, it doesn't.
[doctor] Any pain with flexion and extension of your left arm?
[patient] No, it doesn't.
[doctor] Alright. Let's talk about your medications. You're taking colchicine for your gout. Is that correct?
[patient] Yes, I am.
[doctor] And you're taking that 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for flare-ups?
[patient] Yes, that's correct.
[doctor] Okay. How about any other medications?
[patient] No, just that.
[doctor] Alright. Any questions or concerns about your medications?
[patient] No, I'm good.
[doctor] Alright. Based on your exam today, it looks like you have some swelling and inflammation in your right olecranon. We're going to order an x-ray of that. We're also going to prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day for the pain and swelling in your right elbow.
[patient] Okay.
[doctor] We'll continue the colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for flare-ups of your gout. And you're doing well with your psoriasis, so we'll continue the steroid cream for that.
[patient] Alright.
[doctor] Any questions or concerns about the plan?
[patient] No, I think that sounds good.
[doctor] Alright. I'll have the nurse come in and get you set up for that x-ray. Do you have any other questions or concerns?
[patient] No, I think that's it.
[doctor] Alright. Thank you for coming in today. We'll see you again soon.
[patient] Thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
