dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning. how are you doing today?
[patient] good morning. i'm doing well, thank you.
[doctor] good. so i see that you're here for your annual exam. how are you doing?
[patient] i'm doing well. i've been doing well. i've been working at the bakery this summer.
[doctor] oh, that sounds nice. how's that going?
[patient] it's been good. it's been a lot of fun.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing with your diabetes?
[patient] my diabetes has been doing well. my blood sugars have been fluctuating a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and how do you attribute that to?
[patient] i think it's because of my diet. i've been eating a lot of sweets.
[doctor] okay. how many sweets are you eating?
[patient] i'm trying to cut back on that.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking your medication?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] good. have you missed any doses?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. and how about your blood pressure?
[patient] my blood pressure has been good.
[doctor] okay. and you're still taking your metformin?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] good. how many times a day are you taking it?
[patient] twice a day.
[doctor] okay. and are you sleeping well?
[patient] yes, i am. i've been sleeping about eight hours.
[doctor] okay. and any thoughts of self-harm or suicidal ideations?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. good. so let's go ahead and do a physical exam. so on your physical exam, your grip strength is equal bilaterally. your neurologically, you're intact. your neck is supple, no thyromegaly or lymphadenopathy. no carotid bruits appreciable. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. your heart exam, you have a regular rate. you have a grade 2/6 systolic ejection fraction murmur. no gallops or rubs. no extra heart sounds. good pulses. so let's look at your results. your hemoglobin a1c is elevated. so i know you mentioned that your blood sugars have been fluctuating. are you checking your fasting blood glucose levels each morning?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to encourage you to do that. it's good to check those every morning. call them in about two weeks. we'll see how you're doing. and then we'll discuss further treatment recommendations. you're currently taking metformin twice a day. is that correct?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to continue that. and for your blood pressure, you're currently taking lisinopril ten milligrams once daily. is that correct?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to continue that as well. so do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i think you covered everything.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, i'll see you back in about two months.
[patient] okay. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
