dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, anna. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i've been having some joint pain.
[doctor] okay. so, you've been having some joint pain. what's going on with that?
[patient] well, my left elbow has been really bothering me. i sit at my desk all day for work with my elbows bent. after work, it's really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow. it's really stiff and painful. i've also noticed some swelling on the olecranon of my elbow.
[doctor] okay. i see. have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. and any weakness in your arm?
[patient] yes, i do have some weakness in my arm, but nothing too significant.
[doctor] okay. and any fever or chills?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. let's talk about your past medical history. you have a history of epilepsy. have you had any recent seizures?
[patient] no, i have not had any recent seizures. my last seizure was about a year ago.
[doctor] okay. and you're still taking keppra?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. how about depression? how are you doing with that?
[patient] well, i started therapy last year and i'm trying to avoid medications for this problem. therapy has been helpful, but i still feel down and stressed. i don't have any suicidal or homicidal ideations.
[doctor] okay. and how about your peptic ulcer? how are you doing with that?
[patient] well, i was dealing with a lot of stress last year. i then underwent an endoscopy and it showed that i had an episode of gastritis. i was subsequently diagnosed with peptic ulcer disease and started protonix. i have not had any issues with my ulcer since the procedure and everything has been good.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting?
[patient] no, i have not. i do have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.
[doctor] okay. let's go over some systems. any chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting?
[patient] no.
[doctor] respiratory?
[patient] no.
[doctor] cardiovascular?
[patient] no.
[doctor] musculoskeletal?
[patient] yes, my left elbow joint pain, swelling, and weakness.
[doctor] psychiatric?
[patient] yes, depression.
[doctor] okay. let's go ahead and do a physical exam. let's start with your musculoskeletal exam. your left elbow examination reveals erythema and edema. there is pain to palpation of the left olecranon. it's warm to palpation. there is pain with flexion and extension. palpable left radial pulse. any other issues?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to go ahead and order an x-ray of your left arm. i want to check for any fractures. we'll also get a repeat endoscopy to check on that peptic ulcer. i'm also going to order some labs. i'm going to go ahead and start you on meloxicam 15 milligrams once daily. i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on. you can also ice the area. i think you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma. you have been doing well on keppra. i'm going to continue you on that 500 milligrams twice a day. i will refill that today. you have been doing well with your therapy. i'm going to start you on lexapro 10 milligrams once daily. and for your peptic ulcer disease, we'll continue you on protonix 40 milligrams once daily before meals. any questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i understand.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. great. i'll have my nurse come in and get you checked out. thank you, anna.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
