[doctor] okay. so, let me go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so, let's start with your vital signs. your blood pressure is 124 over 80. your heart rate is 64. your respiratory rate is 18. you weigh 174 pounds and you have no pain. so, let's do a quick exam. so, your shunt site looks good. it's clean, dry, and intact and confirmed at a setting of 2.0. let's talk about your neuro exam. so, your mental status is that you were able to converse easily with me. you were able to spell and do some calculations. you scored 26 out of 30 on the mini-mental status exam. you were able to get two of the three memory words with cuing and the third one with multiple choice. so, that's a slight improvement from your initial score. your gait, let's talk about that. you were able to walk without an assistive device and you scored a gait score of 6 to 8 out of 12 and a balance score of 12 out of 16 for a total score of 18 to 20 out of 28. that's a slight improvement from your initial score of 15 to 17 out of 28. so, your cranial nerves are intact. your pupils are equal. your extraocular movements are intact. your face is symmetric. no dysarthria. your motor is normal for bulk and strength. your coordination is slow for finger-to-nose. so, let's talk about your review of systems. so, have you had any fever or unintentional weight loss?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. any genital sores or decreased or painful output?
