[patient] yes, i had an abnormal pap smear around the age of 20.
[doctor] okay. and then have you had any other pap smears since then?
[patient] yes, i've had normal pap smears since then. the last one was about six months ago.
[doctor] okay. okay. so, have you had any other std's in the past?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. okay. so, i'm gon na go ahead and do a physical exam. i'm gon na start with a pelvic exam. i'm gon na look at your external genitalia, your labia majora and labia minora. i'm gon na check your vaginal opening, and then i'm gon na do a pelvic exam to check your cervix, your vaginal wall, and your uterus. and then i'm gon na take some swabs to check for std's. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, let's go ahead and start with the pelvic exam. so, i'm gon na touch your abdomen here. i'm gon na move my fingers down. i'm gon na feel your uterus and your ovaries. everything feels normal there. i'm gon na move down to your vagina. i'm gon na feel your vaginal opening, and everything looks normal. i'm gon na go ahead and insert my fingers into your vagina. i'm gon na feel your cervix. i'm gon na check your vaginal wall. everything looks normal. there's no cervical motion tenderness or masses noted. so, i'm gon na take some swabs now. i'm gon na take a swab of your cervix, and then i'm gon na take a swab of your vaginal opening. these swabs will be sent to the lab for std testing.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na order a full spectrum std test, which includes gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. we'll call you with the results of the laboratory testing. okay?
