[patient] no, i haven't seen him.
[doctor] okay. so we're going to do a few things today. we're going to do a fluid aspiration and a steroid injection to your right knee. we'll also do an x-ray of your knee and refer you to physical therapy.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm going to explain some of the risks of the steroid injection. the risks include, but are not limited to, hypopigmentation, soft tissue atrophy, tendon ruptures, and transient hyperglycemia, among others.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] do you have any questions about those?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. so we'll go ahead and do the procedure. the procedure is going to be done through the lateral approach, and we'll inject three milliliters of initially clear fluid, then blood-tinged fluid, and then we'll inject eighty milligrams of triamcinolone and one milliliter of lidocaine. does that sound okay?
[patient] yes, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. we'll go ahead and get started. does that sound okay?
[patient] yes, that's fine.
[doctor] okay. so the procedure was done well and there were no complications.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm going to go ahead and prescribe you some xeljanz xr eleven milligrams daily, and you'll continue celebrex two hundred milligrams daily.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] we'll also check your cmp levels and monitor periodically every couple of months. does that sound okay?
[patient] yes, that sounds okay.
[doctor] okay. so for your right knee pain, you have pain and swelling, and your pain level is a six out of ten. on your exam today, your right knee continues to be hot, which is ongoing inflammation. we performed a fluid aspiration today, and we gave you a steroid injection to your right knee. we'll arrange for an x-ray of your right knee and refer you to physical therapy.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] for your lower extremity pitting edema, you noted whole right leg swelling since the last visit. you usually wear support hose, which helps to some degree, and you haven't seen your primary care physician. we discussed compression stockings, elevate your feet, and a low salt diet. you will check with your primary care physician for further instructions.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] do you have any other questions?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. great. take care, nelson.
[patient] thank you, doctor.
[doctor] bye.
[patient] bye. }}<|eot_id|>
