[doctor] okay. let me just do a quick physical exam. i'm going to listen to your heart and lungs. i'm going to check your knee. i'm going to feel your knee. i'm going to check your ankle. your heart and lungs are clear. your knee does have some swelling. it does have some effusion. i'm not feeling any pain with palpation of your lateral knee. your varus test is positive. you do have full range of motion. i'm going to do a lachman's test. that's negative. let me just check your ankle. your dorsalis pedis and posterior tibialis pulses are intact. i'm going to order some x-rays of your knee. i'm going to take four views of your knee. i'm just going to take a look at your x-rays. i don't see any fractures or dislocations or any bony abnormalities. so based on my exam and your x-rays, it looks like you have a right knee lateral collateral ligament strain. i'm going to put you in a walking boot and i want you to follow up with physical therapy. i'm going to prescribe you meloxicam 15 milligrams. take one tablet twice a day. if your pain doesn't improve with physical therapy, i'm going to recommend getting an mri. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i think you covered everything.
