dialogue is: {{ [doctor]: Hi there, how are you doing today?

[patient]: Hi, I'm doing okay, thanks. I'm here for my follow-up appointment.

[doctor]: Great, let's get started. I see you're here for a follow-up of your chronic problem. Can you tell me a bit more about what's been going on?

[patient]: Sure. My osteoarthritis has been flaring up a little lately, especially in my elbows.

[doctor]: Ah, I see. And which elbow is bothering you more, the left or the right?

[patient]: My right elbow bothers me more.

[doctor]: Okay, is it related to your job or any specific activities that you think might be contributing to the flare up?

[patient]: I've been sitting at my computer a lot more at the office, so I'm not sure if it's from sitting in the same position all day.

[doctor]: I see. And do you have any other joint pain besides the elbows?

[patient]: No, just the elbows.

[doctor]: Alright. You also mentioned some numbness and tingling in your hands. Can you tell me more about that?

[patient]: Yes, I get numbness and tingling in my hands, especially if I've been sitting for a while. I try to shake my arms to relieve the numbness.

[doctor]: Hmm, that doesn't sound pleasant. Have you noticed any other issues with your joints or any other symptoms?

[patient]: No, just the numbness and tingling, and the joint pain in my elbows.

[doctor]: Okay. You also have a history of gout. Can you tell me about that?

[patient]: Yes, I had an episode about three months ago. It was inflammation in my toe.

[doctor]: Oh, I see. Did the medication help with that?

[patient]: Yes, the medication helped, and I haven't had any other flare-ups since.

[doctor]: Good to hear. You're still on colchicine for flare-ups, correct?

[patient]: Yes, I take colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed.

[doctor]: Alright. How about your psoriasis? How's that been?

[patient]: It's been under control. I haven't had any major issues with it.

[doctor]: Okay. Let's go over a few other systems. How's your respiratory system been?

[patient]: My lungs feel fine.

[doctor]: And your cardiovascular system?

[patient]: My heart is fine.

[doctor]: Okay. How about your gastrointestinal system?

[patient]: My stomach is fine.

[doctor]: Alright. Let's check your musculoskeletal system. Any swelling or pain in your joints?

[patient]: No, my joints feel okay except for the elbows.

[doctor]: I see. Let's do a quick physical exam. Your neck is supple without any lymph nodes, your lungs are clear, your heart rate and rhythm are regular, your abdomen is soft, and there's no swelling in your lower extremities. Now, let's take a look at your right elbow.

[patient]: Okay.

[doctor]: I see some edema and inflammation around the olecranon. There's tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. Can you move your right arm for me?

[patient]: Sure.

[doctor]: Let's see how it feels. Can you pronate and supinate your arm?

[patient]: It hurts.

[doctor]: And can you flex and extend your arm?

[patient]: Yes, it hurts.

[doctor]: Alright, let's order an x-ray of your right elbow to see if there's any structural issues. We'll also prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day to help with the pain and swelling. We'll continue you on colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for any flare-ups of your gout. You're also still on steroid cream for your psoriasis, and that will continue.

[patient]: Okay, that sounds good.

[doctor]: Do you understand and agree with the recommended medical treatment plan?

[patient]: Yes, I understand and agree.

[doctor]: Great. We'll schedule the x-ray and get you started on the new medication. You'll follow up with me in a few weeks to check on how you're doing. Any questions or concerns?

[patient]: No, I think that's it.

[doctor]: Alright, thank you for coming in today. Take care and we'll see you soon.

[patient]: Thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
