dialogue is: {{ [doctor] Good morning, how are you doing today?

[patient] Hi, I'm okay, thanks. I'm here because of some back pain.

[doctor] I see. What's been going on with your back?

[patient] Well, I was at a birthday party yesterday and I ran into the railing of the staircase and twisted my back. Ever since then, I've been having a lot of pain.

[doctor] I see. Can you describe the pain you're feeling?

[patient] It's mostly in my lower back. It's been pretty bad.

[doctor] Is the pain radiating down to your legs at all?

[patient] No, it's just in my back.

[doctor] Okay. Does lying flat or twisting motions make the pain worse?

[patient] Yes, those make it worse.

[doctor] Alright. Are you taking any medication for the pain?

[patient] I've been taking ibuprofen.

[doctor] How much ibuprofen are you taking?

[patient] I've been taking 200 mg every 6 hours.

[doctor] I see. Let me review your medical history. Have you had any other medical conditions?

[patient] I have anxiety.

[doctor] Okay. Have you had any surgeries?

[patient] Yes, I had a lumbar fusion a few years ago.

[doctor] Alright. Let me check your back now. Can you lie down for me?

[patient] Sure.

[doctor] How does this feel? Any pain when I move your back?

[patient] No, it doesn't seem to hurt when you move it.

[doctor] Great. Can you lift your leg straight up?

[patient] Yes, I can.

[doctor] Does it hurt when you do that?

[patient] No, it doesn't.

[doctor] And how about sensation? Can you feel the sensation in your feet?

[patient] Yes, I can feel it fine.

[doctor] Alright. I'm going to order some X-rays of your lumbar spine to check for any signs of an acute fracture.

[patient] Okay.

[doctor] The X-rays show no signs of an acute fracture. There is evidence of the prior lumbar fusion with the hardware in good position.

[patient] Oh, good to hear.

[doctor] Based on the exam and the X-rays, it looks like you have a lumbar spine strain. This is a common condition that can be caused by the kind of twisting and bending you did when you ran into the railing.

[patient] Okay, what can I do about it?

[doctor] I recommend using ice and heat to help with the pain. You can try alternating between ice and heat to see what works best for you.

[patient] Alright.

[doctor] I also recommend taking Motrin 800 mg 3 times a day with food. This should help with the pain and inflammation.

[patient] I'll do that.

[doctor] It's also important to follow up with me as needed. If the pain doesn't improve or worsens, we may need to consider other treatments.

[patient] I'll follow up if it doesn't get better.

[doctor] Great. Is there anything else you'd like to discuss or any other questions you have?

[patient] No, that's all.

[doctor] Alright, I'll see you again if you need it. Take care and feel better soon.

[patient] Thank you, I appreciate it. }}<|eot_id|>
