dialogue is: {{ [doctor] Hi there, how are you doing today?

[patient] I'm doing alright, thanks. I've been having some shoulder pain.

[doctor] I see. What's been going on with your shoulder?

[patient] I hurt it playing football a few days ago. I was tackled a couple of times and landed on my right shoulder.

[doctor] Oh, sorry to hear that. Can you tell me more about what happened?

[patient] Sure. I was playing pick up football and got tackled a couple of times. I landed on my right shoulder and it really hurt.

[doctor] That sounds like it could be quite painful. How has the pain been since then?

[patient] It's been there ever since. It's on the back of my shoulder.

[doctor] Okay, let's go over the details. Are you feeling any numbness or tingling in your fingers?

[patient] No, I don't feel any numbness or tingling in my fingers.

[doctor] How about the strength in your hand? Is it okay?

[patient] Yes, the strength in my hand is okay, but I've been trying to avoid lifting anything heavy because it hurts too much.

[doctor] Alright, I see. Can you touch your shoulder to your ear?

[patient] No, I can't do that because it hurts too much.

[doctor] That sounds like there might be some limitation in your range of motion. Have you been taking any medication for the pain?

[patient] Yes, I've been taking Tylenol, but it doesn't really help.

[doctor] Okay. Do you have any neck problems or other joint problems?

[patient] No, I don't have any neck problems or other joint problems.

[doctor] Have you had any previous injuries to your right shoulder?

[patient] No, I haven't had any previous injuries to my right shoulder.

[doctor] Any fever or chills since the injury?

[patient] No, I haven't had any fever or chills.

[doctor] Did you hit your head during the injury?

[patient] Yes, I hit my head a little bit, but I didn't pass out.

[doctor] Alright. Let's go over your medical history. Have you had any surgeries?

[patient] Yes, I had an appendectomy about 3 to 4 years ago.

[doctor] Thank you for sharing that. Now, let's go over your systems. How have you been feeling overall?

[patient] I've been feeling okay, no fever or chills.

[doctor] Any muscle or joint pain besides your shoulder?

[patient] No, just the shoulder.

[doctor] Any neurological symptoms like headaches?

[patient] Yes, I've had a headache since the injury.

[doctor] Okay, let's move on to your vital signs. Your blood pressure is 122/76, heart rate is 82 bpm, and oxygen saturation is 95% on room air. Let's do a physical exam now. Can you lift your arms up for me?

[patient] Sure.

[doctor] Can you touch your ear to your shoulder?

[patient] No, it hurts too much.

[doctor] Alright. Let's check your neck. Is there any tenderness to palpation?

[patient] No, there's no tenderness.

[doctor] Your head looks fine, no trauma, no ecchymosis or bruising. Now, let's examine your right shoulder. Can you move your shoulder for me?

[patient] Sure.

[doctor] There's pain to palpation at the acromioclavicular joint. Your abduction and adduction are limited to about 90 degrees. There's pain with supination and pronation of the right arm. Your radial artery pulse is palpable. How does that feel?

[patient] It hurts a lot.

[doctor] I see. We've ordered an x-ray of your right shoulder. The results show an acute acromioclavicular joint fracture.

[patient] Oh, that's not good.

[doctor] Yes, it's a fracture. I'm going to recommend that you wear a sling to support your shoulder. I'll also prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day to help with the pain. Additionally, we'll need to get a CT scan of your right shoulder to evaluate it further.

[patient] Okay, that sounds good.

[doctor] It's also important to avoid tackle football for now. Have you played football before?

[patient] Yes, I play it regularly.

[doctor] Alright, we'll also recommend formal physical therapy to strengthen your right shoulder to help avoid surgery in the future.

[patient] That sounds like a good idea.

[doctor] Great. We'll get you set up with the physical therapy. Do you have any other questions?

[patient] No, I think that's it.

[doctor] Alright. We'll get everything scheduled and follow up with you in a few days to check on your progress. Do you have any other medical concerns or questions?

[patient] No, I don't think so.

[doctor] Alright. We'll see you soon. Take care and follow the instructions I gave you.

[patient] Thank you, doctor. I will.

[doctor] You're welcome. Bye for now.

[patient] Bye. }}<|eot_id|>
