[patient]: No, nothing else.

[doctor]: Alright. Let's move on to your family history. Do you have any family members with any medical conditions?

[patient]: My family runs a bakery. My parents are both diabetic, but my siblings are healthy.

[doctor]: Thank you for that information. Now, about your medications. You mentioned you take metformin. How many tablets do you take each day?

[patient]: I take two tablets twice a day.

[doctor]: Okay, got it. Now, let's do a quick review of your systems. How about your eyes? Any redness, discharge, or icterus?

[patient]: No, my eyes are fine.

[doctor]: Good. How about your ears? Any issues with hearing or ear pain?

[patient]: No, my ears are okay.

[doctor]: Excellent. Let's move on to your respiratory system. Do you have any shortness of breath or cough?

[patient]: No, I don't have any breathing issues.

[doctor]: Okay. How about your cardiovascular system? Any chest pain or palpitations?

[patient]: No, my heart is fine.

[doctor]: Great. Now, let's do a physical exam. I'll start with your eyes again. Everything looks normal there.

[patient]: Yes, they're fine.

[doctor]: Next, I'll examine your ears. Your auditory canal and tympanic membranes are clear.

[patient]: Good to hear that.

[doctor]: Now, let's move on to your respiratory system. I'll listen to your lungs. They sound clear bilaterally.

[patient]: That's good to know.

[doctor]: Next, I'll examine your cardiovascular system. Your heart sounds regular and has a normal rhythm.

[patient]: Okay, that's reassuring.

[doctor]: Now, let's examine your musculoskeletal system. I'll start by palpating your upper back. It doesn't seem to be painful.

[patient]: That's good.

[doctor]: Next, I'll palpate your midline of your lower back. You have some pain here, especially on the left side. There's no pain on the right side. I also notice that when I straighten your leg, it's mildly painful on the right, and more painful on the left.

[patient]: Hmm, that sounds like the pain is worse on the left.

[doctor]: Yes, it is. I'll also do a straight leg raise test. This is mildly positive on the right, and more positive on the left.

[patient]: Okay.

[doctor]: Based on your symptoms and the physical exam, I believe you have a musculoskeletal low back strain. I don't expect to see anything significant on an x-ray, but we will order one to rule out any possible disc issues.

[patient]: Alright, that makes sense.

[doctor]: I'll also refer you to physical therapy to help with the pain and strengthen some of the muscles in your back. It's important to be careful while taking medications, especially muscle relaxers, if you do any strenuous or hazardous activities like driving.

[patient]: I understand. I'll be careful.

[doctor]: I'll order a low back x-ray and also prescribe 400 mg of ibuprofen up to three times a day. You can use Tylenol if the pain is severe. Additionally, I'll prescribe Flexeril.

[patient]: Okay, thank you.

[doctor]: How about your diabetes? How have you been managing it?

[patient]: I've been trying to maintain a healthy lifestyle and avoid foods high in sugar.

[doctor]: That's good to hear. Your hemoglobin A1c is due for an update. I'll order another one. Continue with your diet and exercise, and keep taking your current dose of metformin for now. Also, please check your blood sugar in the morning and log it for me.

[patient]: Alright, I'll do that.

[doctor]: Any questions or concerns about the plan?

[patient]: No, I think I understand everything. Thank you for explaining.

[doctor]: You're welcome. Do you have any questions about the physical therapy or the medications?

[patient]: No, I think I'll be fine.

[doctor]: Alright. We'll get the x-ray scheduled and you'll start with physical therapy soon. If you have any concerns or need any further assistance, don't hesitate to contact us.

[patient]: Thank you, I'll follow up with you if anything changes.

[doctor]: Great. Take care and see you soon.

[patient]: Thank you, doctor. Bye.

[doctor]: Bye. }}<|eot_id|>
