[patient] Yes, I've been feeling really tired.

[doctor] Okay. How about your diet and exercise? Have you been following any specific diets or exercising regularly?

[patient] No, I haven't been exercising much. I've been eating pretty much the same as usual.

[doctor] Alright. Have you noticed any changes in your blood sugar levels?

[patient] Yes, my blood sugars have been running better than they were, but they're still in the 200's.

[doctor] That's good to hear. Your last hemoglobin A1C was 10, correct?

[patient] Yes, that's right.

[doctor] Alright. Let's go ahead and check your vital signs. No fever noted. Your vital signs look good today.

[patient] Okay.

[doctor] Now, let's examine your foot. I see a 1.0 cm x 2.0 cm wound on the dorsal aspect of the lateral right foot, just proximal to the 5th MTP joint. There is some yellow slough present with minimal granulation tissue. No surrounding erythema or cellulitis, no fluid collection, no necrosis, and no odor. No bony exposure, and there's no pain to palpation.

[patient] Okay.

[doctor] We also did an X-ray of your right foot today, and there's no evidence of osteomyelitis.

[patient] Alright.

[doctor] Based on your history and the examination, I've diagnosed you with a right diabetic foot ulcer. We'll need to do some further testing to determine the blood flow to your foot. We can do an ankle brachial index, which will help us understand how well your blood is circulating to the affected area.

[patient] Alright, that sounds good.

[doctor] I also recommend a debridement in the office today to help clean and prepare the wound. Would you be comfortable with that?

[patient] Yes, I'll do it.

[doctor] Great. We'll also prescribe collagenase ointment for you to apply to the wound once a day, and cover it with a sterile dressing. You should continue this until we see the ulcer decrease in size.

[patient] Okay.

[doctor] Additionally, I recommend you wear a surgical shoe to provide increased support for your foot.

[patient] Alright, I can do that.

[doctor] You'll need to follow up with me in 2 weeks to check on your progress. Do you have any questions or concerns about the treatment plan?

[patient] No, I don't think so. Thank you.

[doctor] You're welcome. We'll see you in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
